1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,252
Carpal tunnel syndrome causes tingling, aching pain in your wrist and fingers.

2
00:00:04,572 --> 00:00:09,941
It happens when the tunnel around your median nerve gets squeezed — and these three habits are the biggest culprits.

3
00:00:10,261 --> 00:00:13,286
First, holding your phone with your wrist bent for long stretches.

4
00:00:13,606 --> 00:00:19,111
Every extra hour of smartphone use in that bent position adds more strain to the nerve running through the tunnel.

5
00:00:19,431 --> 00:00:22,456
Second, typing or using a mouse without wrist support.

6
00:00:22,776 --> 00:00:26,917
Bending your wrist up or sideways keeps steady pressure on that nerve all day.

7
00:00:27,237 --> 00:00:30,113
Finally, sleeping with your wrist curled under your pillow.

8
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:38,454
Blood flow slows at night, so that bent position squeezes the nerve even harder, which is why so many wake up with numb, tingling hands.

9
00:00:38,774 --> 00:00:39,444
Here's the fix.

10
00:00:39,764 --> 00:00:44,141
Keep your wrist straight when you hold your phone, and stretch every 20 to 30 minutes.

11
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,556
Add a wrist rest to your keyboard and mouse.

12
00:00:46,876 --> 00:00:50,658
And wear a wrist splint at night to keep your wrist from curling while you sleep.
